{{> Logo this}}

{{> EmailTitle title=(t "Confirm Your New Email Address") }}

{{!--
  Sent to the new address when someone asks to make it their account's
  (#9821, Common's EmailChangeConfirmation). The account keeps its old
  address until this link is opened, so the address is proven before it
  can be used to sign in or to reset the password. The reader may not be
  the person who asked - someone may have typed this address by mistake -
  so it says what happens if they ignore it.

  In the language on the account that asked (#10157): the reader of a new
  address is most often its own person. The product's name is the
  installation's own (brandName), so it goes into a sentence through
  ttHtml, which escapes the whole sentence; the request's rows are values.
  Everything else is OneUptime's own words, looked up in the reader's
  language (Utils/EmailLanguage.ts).
--}}

{{> InfoBlock info=(ttHtml "Someone asked to make this the email address of their {{product}} account. If that was you, confirm it with the button below." product=(brandName))}}

{{> ButtonBlock buttonUrl=tokenVerifyUrl buttonText=(t "Confirm Email Address")}}

{{> VerticalSpace this}}

{{> LinkBlock linkUrl=tokenVerifyUrl linkLabel=(t "Or copy and paste this link into your browser:")}}

{{> VerticalSpace this}}

{{#if requestedAt}}
{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "Details of the request:")}}

{{> DetailBoxStart this }}
{{> DetailBoxField title=(t "Requested at:") plainText=requestedAt }}
{{> RequestOriginFields this }}
{{> DetailBoxEnd this }}
{{/if}}

{{> InfoBlock plainInfo=(tp "This link works for {{count}} hour, and only once." "This link works for {{count}} hours, and only once." expiresInHours)}}

{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "Didn't ask for this? You can safely ignore this email. Nothing changes unless the link above is opened.")}}

{{> SupportBlock this }}

